$select — pick elements from input arrays by index

SUMMARY
  Copies selected indices from named input arrays to output. All other
  arrays are empty in the result.

SYNTAX
  $select(sounds=[1])
  $select(texts=[2], sounds=[0, 1, 2])
  $select(text=[2], sounds=[0, 1, 2])   — singular aliases (text, sound, image, …)
  $select(sounds=@indices)   — indexes from @indices texts[]

INPUT
  Any arrays referenced in (...).

OUTPUT
  Only the listed arrays, each containing the selected links in order.

ARGUMENTS
  array=[i, j, ...] — zero-based indexes into that input array.
  array=@ref — each text from @ref is one index (supports key=@list output).

EXAMPLE
  @vocals: @track -> $music_separation(model=2stem)
  @mm: @vocals -> $select(sounds=[1]) -> $change_voice(model=MuscleMan)

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  No.
